          ],
          "text": "You were found on the floor after a fall on the way to the commode. You could not remember all of what happened.\n\nWhile you were in hospital, the team also found:\n\n- A possible chest infection (aspiration pneumonia)\n- Inflammation in part of your bowel (sigmoid diverticulitis)\n- A patch on your right lung (consolidation)\n- Your kidneys were not working as well as usual (acute kidney injury, or AKI)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team ran a number of tests. These included blood tests, urine tests, heart tracings (ECGs), and scans of your head, neck, chest and abdomen. One scan showed some changes in your bowel and a patch on your lung.\n\nTo treat you, the team gave you:\n\n- A strong antibiotic drip called Tazocin (piperacillin-tazobactam)\n- Fluids through a drip\n- Oxygen"
        },
        {
